== 4. Testing the scaler: open-loop burst vs closed-loop clients (same 120 s window; the closed loops are NOT offered the burst) ==
  open loop (Poisson, 20 req/s burst): peak outstanding  1301  p99 wait    60.9 s  attain 0.397  peak replicas 100
  closed loop,  8 clients, think 3.0 s: peak outstanding     8  p99 wait     0.1 s  attain 1.000  peak replicas 3
  closed loop, 64 clients, think 0.5 s: peak outstanding    64  p99 wait    19.7 s  attain 0.982  peak replicas 22
  A closed loop can only ever have `clients` requests outstanding. It exercises the scaler only if clients >= the demand you want to test, and its arrival rate falls as latency rises.

